cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cy23 in your work, please cite the specific version used."
title: "cy23: A Python toolkit for thermodynamic gas-turbine cycle modeling"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ferrer-Vidal España-Heredia"
    given-names: "Luis"
    email: "luis.ferrer-vidal@erau.edu"
version: "2026.11"
date-released: 2026-11-06
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24026309
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/ferrervidal/cy23"
abstract: >-
  cy23 is a Python toolkit for thermodynamic gas-turbine cycle modeling,
  including thermally perfect gas calculations, turbomachinery map handling,
  customizable engine architectures, steady-state cycle matching, bleed-flow
  arrangements, and multi-operating-point analysis.
keywords:
  - gas-turbine cycle modeling
  - engine performance
  - turbomachinery
  - thermodynamics
  - cycle analysis
